==============================================================================
  Mutation tests  (assertion-strength validation)
==============================================================================

  Strategy: replace each named fact's body with `{}` (no constraint),
  then re-run Alloy. Each listed assertion should now FAIL on the
  mutated model. If it still PASSes, the assertion is vacuous and
  must be strengthened.

  - MUTATE F_AuditImmutable  → runs/B-L3/mutated_F_AuditImmutable.als
    rationale: Removing this fact allows the model to invent a state where an AuditEntry is modified (same task, actor, operation but different entry), which is exactly what the AppendOnly and AuditImmutable assertions are supposed to catch.
    expected to FAIL: FR_017_AuditImmutable, AppendOnly
      - FR_017_AuditImmutable: FAIL (expected)
      - AppendOnly: FAIL (expected)

  - MUTATE F_OwnerOnlyShareControl  → runs/B-L3/mutated_F_OwnerOnlyShareControl.als
    rationale: Removing this fact lets the model invent a share where the sharee equals the owner, violating the ownership-based access control pattern. This tests that only the owner can control the share list.
    expected to FAIL: FR_010_OwnerOnlyShareControl, OwnershipBasedAccess
      - FR_010_OwnerOnlyShareControl: FAIL (expected)
      - OwnershipBasedAccess: FAIL (expected)

  - MUTATE F_NoTeamSharing  → runs/B-L3/mutated_F_NoTeamSharing.als
    rationale: Removing this fact allows the model to invent cross-team shares, violating FR-012. The assertion checks that all sharees belong to the same team as the task owner.
    expected to FAIL: FR_012_NoTeamSharing
      - FR_012_NoTeamSharing: PASS (vacuous?)

  - MUTATE F_CrossTeamIsolation  → runs/B-L3/mutated_F_CrossTeamIsolation.als
    rationale: Removing this fact lets the model invent a state where a user from a different team can access (share or ownership) a task, directly violating the cross-team isolation guarantee and byte-equivalent 404 requirements.
    expected to FAIL: FR_006_CrossTeamIsolation, NoInformationLeakage, FR_014_ByteEquivalentNotFound
      - FR_006_CrossTeamIsolation: PASS (vacuous?)
      - NoInformationLeakage: PASS (vacuous?)
      - FR_014_ByteEquivalentNotFound: PASS (vacuous?)

  - MUTATE F_AuditCompleteness  → runs/B-L3/mutated_F_AuditCompleteness.als
    rationale: Removing this fact lets the model invent a task with a TaskOwnership but no corresponding Created audit entry, violating the requirement that every task mutation produces an audit entry.
    expected to FAIL: FR_015_AuditCompleteness, AuditCompleteness
      - FR_015_AuditCompleteness: FAIL (expected)
      - AuditCompleteness: FAIL (expected)

